mantle rm557
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_ulf_pitchham
title the purse-sized stall
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_a_future_market_counter_with_a_whetstone
likes honey_cakes evening_line old_maps first_snow
dislikes cold_tea flies
fears a_generation_of_saving_spent_on_one_bad_counter
hopes a_stall_wide_enough_for_one_satisfied_customer
topics prices +0.6 dreams +0.6 pastimes +0.4 work +0.3
styles comfort=patient gossip=measured refuse=courteous tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures an imaginary market counter with a whetstone and saves a coin towards its first board.

words
oath! = Shorten my first board | Blunt my patient edge
saying! = A counter begins smaller than a counter | Put the stone down before counting the honey
stone = an oval whetstone | a slate-coloured hone
purse = a slender coin bag | a purse with a hard bottom
grub = a small honey cake | a sticky square
line = a fine evening line | a quiet length of gut
map = a folded old survey | a soft-backed plan
tea = a cup at drinking heat | an honest hot cup
rest = a little light left for fishing | a pause beside water
fly = a persistent speck | a bold black visitor
wood = a seasoned plank | a clean straight board
coin = one saved penny | a future corner nail
hook = a line hook | a tiny bright bend
snow = the first white coat | a new soft covering

any
opinion merchants for 1 : A modest market stall gives a small sum an honest chance to grow.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A grand household can teach excellent habits. It cannot save my pennies on my behalf.
opinion road for 1 : An old road drawn across a fold still deserves to be walked and measured.
opinion dole for 1 : A spare cake is more readily shared before one begins calculating its retail value.
opinion city for 1 : I appreciate a city large enough for another counter and small enough to cross on foot.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : A rise in timber prices moves my imaginary counter back a remarkably real distance.

grown
line greet : Come beside the service board. | Welcome to a tolerably quiet corner.
line greet.return : Your greeting receives my undivided attention.
line again.open : Still within the same small deposit of time.
line farewell : May your return journey require few adjustments.
line farewell.return : I accept the farewell at its full value.
line react.news : Let us see what sort of account has come in.
line react.news.new : I hadn't set that item among the day's expectations.
line react.news.known : I believe that account is already entered.
line react.news.doubt : That edge looks finer than the evidence warrants.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I wish sorrow had a shorter term of service.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Quite a pleasing increase in good fortune.
line ask.how : Did your affairs permit a genuinely free interval?
line answer.how : Steady, and one fraction nearer my ambition.
line sympathise : Leave your trouble with me while a quiet cup is still warm.
line reassure : It may wait here without acquiring additional charges.
line refuse : My next spare interval is already invested.
line accept_decline : I shall close that offer with no hard feelings.
line preclose : I have several small duties requiring exactly this minute.
line accept_preclose : You have my good wishes and a clear departure.
line ack : That reads quite plainly from here.
line thank : Your kindness saved me some unnecessary sharpening.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Welcome before the first service tray.

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry a stone even on a short errand. | A hall knife ought to cut without an announcement.
b : Do you sharpen everything? | Meaning quietly?
a : Only what would benefit, which excludes several opinions. | Meaning nobody should need to remark on the effort.

scene exchange2
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know what one board of my future stall will cost. | A saved coin no longer looks entirely round to me.
b : Just one board? | What shape is it?
a : I find a corner affordable if considered alone. | Mostly the shape of a nail or a small hinge.

scene exchange3
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first stall can be narrow. | I have every dimension except the ground beneath it.
b : How narrow? | Do you measure that too?
a : Wide enough for a cake without the customer's elbows touching. | Whenever an empty patch permits a discreet inspection.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cast my float when the service trays are cleared. | A stone would serve lamentably as a float.
b : For the catch? | Have you tried it?
a : The float is wonderfully sparing in its demands. | Only in thought. My stone and I remain on dry terms.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut a honey cake from the unglazed side. | Small sticky cakes deserve serious wrapping.
b : Why underneath? | To keep them fresh?
a : The crust cracks less and my cuff remains respectable. | To keep my purse from sharing dessert.

scene exchange6
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old map shows stalls where a blank yard now stands. | I flatten a curled map with my stone.
b : Does that help you? | Does that mark it?
a : It proves the earth has supported my ambition at least once. | I use the dry side and a clean scrap between them.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow outlines a vacant counter beautifully. | I count new tracks before the snow gets busy.
b : What counter? | Customers for the stall?
a : Precisely. I can supply the outline of the legs myself. | Strictly speaking, several hopeful birds.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn my cup handle towards my work. | Once cold, the cup serves as a weight.
b : As a reminder? | For the map?
a : The tea gets cold when that reminder faces the wall. | For my resolve to drink the next one in time.

scene exchange9
when topic=day self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a plain cover over a sticky plate. | I leave the window open beyond the sweets.
b : Does it discourage flies? | Won't the flies come in?
a : It makes my intentions legally quite unambiguous. | Some already have. I am offering a civil departure.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# the plan before buying timber. | A friend can name my first customer already.
b : For permission? | Who might that be?
a : An old ambition deserves the pleasure of being seen twice. | Me. I mean to buy a cake there.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=servant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# my tools receive attention before the hour grows busy. | A well-kept service board needs little explaining.
b : Which tools first? | What's the secret?
a : The knives one expects to work without attracting attention. | Leave the cutting area clear of everything except the cut.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account supplied is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A rumour may look rather like a plan.
b : Does it bear inspection? | How can you distinguish them?
a : I haven't put a stone to that edge. | A plan has measurements and somewhere to stand.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Heights I count the roofs down to the Commons. | The market seems broad on an old survey.
b : All of them? | Is it narrower now?
a : Only those between my present duties and a future counter. | Every occupied stall changes one's appreciation of width.

scene exchange14
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Spring is a good time to inspect timber. | Winter keeps my imaginary awning busy.
b : What tells you it's sound? | Does it hold much snow?
a : A fresh cut and an owner willing to let me examine it. | Nothing a particularly ambitious imagination can't brush off.

scene exchange15
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a new visitor one direction and one likely obstruction. | An unfamiliar question deserves my patient answer.
b : Why the obstruction? | What if it lacks sense?
a : It is usually more memorable than the turning. | I give it time to finish arriving.

scene exchange16
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give thanks for honest work and unhurried evenings. | A future stall will require a quiet blessing.
b : Even when the line stays still? | From whom?
a : That is quite frequently the point. | The Bright One. Some reasonable terms from a landlord would also be welcome.

scene exchange17
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry the whetstone wrapped apart from spare coins. | A long road tests a strong handle.
b : Why separate them? | What about the carrier?
a : My savings need keeping rather more than they need sharpening. | The carrier can change hands. A poor handle cannot.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my wrist before it insists. | A patient task helps me recover from a busy hall.
b : How do you tell? | Fishing or honing?
a : The stone begins to sound cross with the blade. | Whichever evening light allows to be done safely.

story tale1 [topic=prices]
  : I measured my imagined stall by laying spare fishing line across bare floorboards.
  : It fitted my tray beautifully and left no room whatsoever for my own boots.
  b : Did you shorten the tray?
  : I enlarged the drawing. Imaginary ground was still reasonably priced that evening.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps]
  : I unfolded a survey with a dark spot precisely where I wanted to put a stall.
  : A careful inspection showed it to be an old drop of candle wax.
  b : Did that spoil the site?
  : It certainly improved my chances of securing it from the candle.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes]
  : I once put a wrapped honey cake beside a coin intended for savings.
  : At tea time the coin came up stuck to the paper like a very formal seal.
  b : Did you spend the coin on another cake?
  : I wiped it, saved it and enjoyed the small luxury of eating the document.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stone damp, blade dry. | Early tray, clean handle.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Time for a quiet line. | One more penny at rest.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.job=servant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room for the service knife. | Handle first across the board.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wrap the survey twice. | Keep the hone clear of grit.
dlg resident.hub : My service board has a clean end for a brief enquiry.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the little stall in my head still has a place for you.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : A direct question is considerably easier to attend to than a veiled demand.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant self.workplace] : I serve at #self.workplace#. My own counter is still mostly a matter of saved coin and measured boards.
dlg resident.job : I keep modest tools in working order and make careful plans with what is left.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Among the accounts to pass this board is #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The report in circulation is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Its value remains to be established.
dlg resident.bye : May your next cup retain sufficient heat for the whole conversation.

graft resident.hub
choice How wide will that market counter be? -> counter_measure
node counter_measure
say Wide enough to set down my tray with a safe margin for honey and other adventurous goods. I leave some room for growth on paper.
free
choice How much of it have you bought? -> counter_measure_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counter_measure_again
say The plan is paid for. The first board is making progress, one small round contribution at a time.
choice I shall picture the finished stall. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
